# M / B007 — add-dependency, angular, api-versioning, architecture-decision.

C R140 OL WF-001 | MUST | Inspect the relevant existing code and read the owning rules before a non-trivial change; rules that have not loaded yet (e.g. dependencies.md before a manifest is opened) are read explicitly. | non-trivial changes | none stated
C R141 OL DEP-002 | MUST NOT | When the approved stack defines a technology for a capability use it rather than silently selecting an alternative; never silently replace a requested package with an alternative. | technology and package choice | none stated
C R142 OL ARC-020,GOV-017 | REQUIRES_APPROVAL (Reserved) | Reserved decisions need explicit approval unless already required by the specification or established structure: changing an accepted project or architecture decision; a new architectural style or pattern (Rich Domain Model or DDD tactical patterns, CQRS/MediatR/Vertical Slice Architecture, event sourcing, microservices); a new production project, layer or assembly or an additional DbContext/persistence boundary; changed persistence boundaries or technology; a new infrastructure category (messaging, background processing, distributed caching, search, external storage, external identity); a major library or framework or replacing an approved baseline technology; a project-wide convention or abstraction (e.g. a project-wide Result model); a new or changed authentication/authorization architecture; a breaking public API change. | consequential decisions | Already required by the specification or established project structure.
C R143 OL DEP-017 | DEFAULT | When Controller API versioning has been explicitly adopted use the Controller integration of Asp.Versioning (Asp.Versioning.Mvc plus Asp.Versioning.Mvc.ApiExplorer for versioned OpenAPI); do not add the package before the project adopts versioning. | API versioning packages | none stated
C R144 OL DEP-004 | MUST | Before installation check whether the selected package/version is deprecated, check known vulnerability information and verify the license of the exact selected version from official registry metadata (and upstream when necessary). | dependency additions and updates | none stated
C R145 OL DEP-005 | REQUIRES_APPROVAL | Do not install automatically a dependency requiring payment or a commercial license, or one whose license has material obligations or cannot be confidently classified; explain the concern, present reasonable alternatives and wait for approval; say so explicitly when no free alternative exists. | dependency additions | Approval given.
C R146 OL WF-007 | MUST | After a dependency change run the manifest check, restore and build the affected projects and inspect vulnerability information for the changed dependency set. | dependency changes | none stated
C R147 OL GOV-014 | MUST | Keep changes focused on the requested scope and preserve existing behavior unless the task or approved specification requires a change (e.g. no automatic replacement or upgrade of unrelated packages because a scanner reports a finding; no unrelated dependency cleanup). | all changes | Task or approved specification requires the change.
C R148 OL GOV-012 | DEFAULT | Prefer simple, maintainable solutions and avoid speculative abstractions (e.g. no custom abstraction around every UI-library component without a concrete reason). | all code | none stated
C R149 OL GOV-013 | MUST NOT | Do not introduce frameworks, libraries, infrastructure or architectural patterns without a concrete current need (e.g. Angular Material is not added automatically to a project that has not chosen it). | all changes | none stated
C R150 OL WF-016 | DEFAULT | Treat generated code as generated: keep it separate from handwritten logic and regenerate it when the source contract changes. | generated clients and outputs | none stated
C R152 OL API-022 | MUST | Deprecating a published API version is a migration process (metadata marking plus the development-workflow deprecation obligations), not merely an attribute. | published API versions | none stated
C R153 OL GOV-017 | MUST | Classify a decision before acting on it: Decided (settled by the product sources, CLAUDE.md, the technology stack, rules, an accepted decision record or established structure; reopening it requires approval), Delegated (local, reversible, no boundary, dependency, convention, contract or observable-behavior change; decide without asking), Reserved (explicit approval). | all consequential choices | none stated
C R154 OL GOV-017 | MUST | For a Reserved decision stop that part of the work and issue a Decision Request (Context, Options, Recommendation, Blocked, Proceeding with) through architecture-decision; continue only with compliant non-Reserved work; an explicit user instruction counts as approval. | Reserved decisions | none stated
C R155 OL GOV-017 | MUST | In an autonomous or headless run never make a Reserved decision: proceed only with the policy-compliant non-Reserved 'Proceeding with' work and report every unresolved Decision Request. | headless runs | none stated
C R156 OL GOV-007 | MUST | When a new behavioral rule or product value is approved, update the durable source of truth in the same change (SPECIFICATION.md, or CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md through custom-settings). | approved product behavior | none stated
C X10 EX DEP-001,GOV-014 | MUST | Remove dependencies that are no longer used when doing so is part of the current change and safe to verify; do not leave dead package references behind. | dependency changes | Unrelated cleanup in a narrowly scoped task. | DEP-001 governs adding dependencies and GOV-014 limits scope; no oracle policy requires removing unused dependencies. | A change that makes a package unused is incomplete until the package reference is removed.
C X11 EX DEP-004,DEP-005,WF-009 | MUST | The add-dependency report states the package, selected version, license, checks performed and approval status (approved / awaiting approval / not needed). | dependency changes | none stated | DEP-004/DEP-005 require the checks and approval gate and WF-009 truthful verification reporting; no oracle policy prescribes the dependency report contents. | A dependency change reported without its license or approval status does not follow the workflow.
C X12 EX GOV-017,GOV-007 | MUST | An approved Reserved decision (including an explicit instruction in the original request) is recorded before its Reserved part is implemented: a record docs/decisions/NNNN-short-title.md with Status, Date, Context, Decision, Alternatives considered and Consequences, plus an update of the planning-time owner (CLAUDE.md Architecture Defaults or docs/technology-stack.md); new path-rule constraints are edited into the owning rule; rejected or deferred decisions worth keeping are recorded with that status. | approved decisions | Product behavior and tunable values go to SPECIFICATION.md / CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md. | GOV-017 requires approval for Reserved decisions but no recording artifact; no oracle policy requires decision records or planning-owner updates. | After approval to adopt a new library the change is incomplete without the decision record and the technology-stack update.

